{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQvwQ1h5bQ1L6P65dW9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `Hijack()` now works after `WriteHeaderNow()` and only refuses once body bytes have been written.\n\n**What was wrong:** commit 32065bb made `Hijack()` return `errHijackAlreadyWritten` as soon as `Written()` was true. That includes the case where only the headers have been sent (`size == 0`). No body bytes are on the wire at that point, and Go's standard HTTP server allows hijacking then (it flushes the headers first). So handlers or middleware that send headers before upgrading a connection were being rejected.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `response_writer.go`: the check is now `w.size > 0` instead of `w.Written()`, with a comment explaining why.\n- `response_writer_test.go`: added a test case, \"hijack after WriteHeaderNow should succeed\".\n\n**Verified:**\n- The new test failed before the fix with `gin: response already written`, and passes after it.\n- The existing hijack tests still pass: hijacking before any write succeeds, and hijacking after a body write still fails.\n- `go vet` and `gofmt` are clean, and `go test ./...` passes in every package.\n\nI haven't committed anything; you're on a detached HEAD. Your message would work as the commit subject if you want me to commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":39482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":747,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7664fac6-847d-4fcc-bd82-b4f55da611ef","uuid":"0e4548ad-b35d-4c13-9cdd-da0657323791","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:29:10.164Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQvwBNwK41fyC7FB64S"}
