then (it flushes the headers first). So handlers or middleware that send headers before upgrading a connection were being rejected.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `response_writer.go`: the check is now `w.size > 0` instead of `w.Written()`, with a comment explaining why.\n- `response_writer_test.go`: added a test case, \"hijack after WriteHeaderNow should succeed\".\n\n**Verified:**\n- The new test failed before the fix with `gin: response already written`, and passes after it.\n- The existing hijack tests still pass: hijacking before any write succeeds, and hijacking after a body write still fails.\n- `go vet` and `gofmt` are clean, and `go test ./...` passes in every package.\n\nI haven't committed anything; you're on a detached HEAD. Your message would work as the commit subject if you want me to commit.","ttft_ms":4698,"type":"result","duration_ms":32539,"uuid":"c3b49c69-1a12-41a9-a83e-b9c0aa8f6881","ttft_stream_ms":892,"time_to_request_ms":131,"first_content_frame_ms":892,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
